---
import LatexLogo from '../components/LatexLogo.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BooleanTool from '../components/BooleanTool.svelte';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={'Boolean algebra | lab by faris0x'}
  description="Simplify Boolean expressions with truth tables, canonical forms and Quine–McCluskey prime implicants, then export the working as a .tex file."
  current="boolean"
  math
>
  <div class="tool-head">
    <div>
      <h1>Boolean algebra</h1>
    </div>
    <p>
      Turn a Boolean statement into its truth table, canonical forms and a
      minimal sum of products. The finished working exports as <LatexLogo />.
    </p>
  </div>

  <BooleanTool client:idle />

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="reading">
    <h2 id="reading">Reading the result</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The truth table lists every assignment of the variables. Minterms are the
      rows where the statement is true; maxterms are the rows where it is
      false. The canonical forms spell those rows out fully.
    </p>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The simplifier uses the Quine–McCluskey method. It combines adjacent
      minterms into prime implicants, then chooses essential prime implicants
      and a small cover for the rest. The result is a minimal sum of products,
      not merely a different-looking equivalent statement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="syntax">
    <h2 id="syntax">Syntax</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list section-intro">
      <li><strong>Negation</strong>: <code>~p</code> or <code>!p</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Conjunction</strong>: <code>p &amp; q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Disjunction</strong>: <code>p | q</code> or <code>p v q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Exclusive or</strong>: <code>p ^ q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Implication</strong>: <code>p -&gt; q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Equivalence</strong>: <code>p &lt;-&gt; q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Constants</strong>: <code>0</code> and <code>1</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="export">
    <h2 id="export">Export</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The <LatexLogo /> tab previews the document and lets you copy or download
      the <code>.tex</code> source. The export includes the truth table,
      canonical forms, prime implicants and the minimised expression.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
